meta {
  name: Gated site — open a sign-in window
  type: http
  seq: 7
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/connectors/{{scrapeConnector}}/browser/login
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
}

docs {
  Opens a real Chromium window **on the machine running QuickJoiner** so you can sign in
  once; the session is then reused for every sync. Returns immediately (it is a background
  job) — poll `GET .../browser/session` to see when it lands.

  409 when a sign-in window is already open for this connector, or when the host has no
  display (Docker / a remote server) — in that case run `qj browser login <url>` on a
  machine with a desktop that shares the workspace.

  The URL comes from the connector's own `start_urls`, never from the request body: this
  route must not become a way to make the server open an arbitrary page.

  Most SSO sign-ins issue a **session cookie**, which a browser profile cannot retain on
  its own — QuickJoiner captures those explicitly while the window is open, which is what
  makes the sign-in stick.
}
